# =============================================================================
#  Decay with UNKNOWN measurement noise    A --k--> (gone)
# =============================================================================
#  A single first-order decay, A(t) = A0 exp(-k t), from A0 = 100, measured with
#  CONSTANT additive noise of a fixed (but here, "unknown") size. This is the
#  setup for estimating the noise (lesson 36): rather than supplying the
#  measurement error as an _SD column, we let the fit ESTIMATE it jointly with the
#  rate, via `noise_model = normal, sigma = fit <name>`.
#
#  Only k is a model parameter; the noise level is a NUISANCE parameter (a named
#  free variable the noise-model line binds its sigma to), not part of the model.
# =============================================================================

begin model

begin parameters
  k   0.5    # decay rate [1/day]  <- FITTED
  A0  100    # initial amount [AU] (fixed/known)
end parameters

begin molecule types
  A()
end molecule types

begin seed species
  A()  A0
end seed species

begin observables
  Molecules  Obs_A  A()
end observables

begin reaction rules
  A_decay: A() -> 0  k
end reaction rules

end model
